        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">in FMA this is a paired structure. NCITA has &apos;pelvic bone&apos; but this is the *superclass* of ilium/ischium/pubis. The MA class &apos;pelvis bone&apos; is actually a superclass of &apos;pelvic girdle bone&apos; and caudal/sacral vertebra.</owl:annotatedTarget>
