        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The lateral epicondyle of the femur, smaller and less prominent than the medial epicondyle, gives attachment to the fibular collateral ligament of the knee-joint. Directly below it is a small depression from which a smooth well-marked groove curves obliquely upward and backward to the posterior extremity of the condyle.</owl:annotatedTarget>
