        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A zone of bone organ consisting of small pits on the inner surface of the parietal bone, most numerous near the sagittal suture, that lodge the arachnoid granulations (Pacchionian bodies) responsible for reabsorption of cerebrospinal fluid into the dural venous sinuses.</obo:IAO_0000115>
