        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A bone foramen opening on the posterior surface of the petrous part of the temporal bone, transmitting the facial nerve (CN VII), the vestibulocochlear nerve (CN VIII), and the labyrinthine artery from the posterior cranial fossa into the internal acoustic canal. Its fundus is divided into compartments by the transverse crest and Bill&apos;s bar.</obo:IAO_0000115>
