        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A neural arch forming the posterior bony ring of the tenth thoracic vertebra, consisting of pedicles and laminae enclosing the vertebral foramen at the lower thoracic level. T10 is transitional; its arch bears transverse processes that may have a small costal facet for rib 10 and articular processes that begin to reflect the approaching thoracolumbar morphology.</owl:annotatedTarget>
